think Keaton granted %374 mid-lap and said kg then send, so the grant was built in the same round rather than booked. It was already RULED 20260831.115500 with the build left to the roster lane, so the design existed and the word opened it.
think Reds first before the grant: three of the hot pass's nine reds were mine. The ledger headline still read 407 rows against a measured 408, repaired by its own loom rather than by hand -- reds_ledger_headline_write.sh names itself in the refusal. And %408's prose put the word closed within sixty characters of %360, which reads as a claim to close an OPEN row; the word described the Cursor CLI trial, so the sentence took a different verb.
think The gate field is the one roster qualifier a hand types about its own tree, which is exactly what made Keaton right to gate it. So the vocabulary is not kept in the scan: the legal gate numbers are read out of the card's own custody section at scan time. A roster can claim only a gate the card declares, retiring a gate on the card retires every row leaning on it in the same edit, and an unreadable card empties the vocabulary and refuses every gate rather than welcoming them all.
obs The counter split is the whole repair, and it is REDS %338's shape one room over: red had carried both this guard broke and this guard is parked at a gate the maintainer named, and the receipt gate read their sum. red recovers its single meaning; gated says the other thing; only the first refuses.
obs Three refusals hold the field to its meaning, each proven in a pen: an ungated red still reds, still refuses, and still costs the receipt; an absent path is never gated, since a guard whose file is gone proves nothing whatever its row claims; and a gate the card never declares is refused by name. Fifteen new control legs, every one asked in the direction that would make the field a free pass.
obs unheard_guard read 1117 against a ceiling of 1116 -- over by exactly one. The fix was the guard this lap had just repaired: agent_jail rostered at tier lap, host linux, bringing the reading to 1116 and meeting the ceiling. A guard proved green once and heard by nothing guards nothing.
obs A phantom_closure in %374's own text predates this lap -- custody gates wear the same percent sigil as ledger rows, which REDS %375 already booked and whose stripper handles the literal phrase gate %N. The rewrite closed it. The collision itself is real and stands: a gate number and a row number are told apart by one adjacent word.
loom witness=standing_equipment_control legs=21 new_legs=15 wall_s=9
loom scan=standing_equipment gate_parked=5 unknown_gate=0 planted_undeclared=1 unreadable_card_refused=5
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh the gate field parsed, a gated red booked apart from a broken one, and the receipt written past a gated-only close disclosing what it chained past
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scan.sh the gate vocabulary derived from the card's custody section rather than kept here, and the run card's gated verdict no longer counted red
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh fifteen legs, each asked in the direction that would make the field a free pass
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri five gate rows and the repaired agent_jail guard, rostered the lap it was fixed
think Keaton said kg a second time while the hot pass was mid-flight, so the charter's own step 1 was folded into this lap rather than paid for with a second thirty-minute pass. The pass was stopped at 26 of 109 and one pass now covers the whole set.
think Measuring the fleet to write %409's number down is what found %409. The two files were read side by side to count the spellings, and the counts disagreed on the page: six seat names admitted against nine reported, and an elder remap seated that morning present in one file and absent from the other.
obs The drift was across the file boundary rather than inside either file. Four copies live inside fleet-loop.sh and a hand edits those together; the two that parted are the ones in the other file. A copy you can see is a copy you maintain, and a copy in another file is a copy you forget.
obs The reader printed its answer twice on the first draft: awk exit jumps to END and the END flushed the same record again. Invisible to a caller reading one line and a fault to one reading all of them, so the record is cleared before the exit and a control leg asserts the answer is exactly one line.
obs status parked is the field that lets the six aether seats stay readable without pretending they run, since an absent directory is a filesystem accident where a parked row is a declaration. engine field is a word rather than a blank for the same reason: the interactive bench refuses an unattended lap by name instead of falling into a claude branch that would start one.
obs The sharpest control leg is the one that watches for the fault coming back: a seat name surviving in a case arm of the loop is a seventh copy being born, and the guard greps for exactly that.
obs Two REDS folds this lap, and the ledger headline repaired twice by its own loom rather than by hand. The card ran 765 bytes over at one point and every addition was paid for by condensing a block that had had its day -- which is the structural finding it is worth naming rather than the byte-shaving it looks like.
loom witness=fleet_roster legs=17 wall_s=3 pen_cases=2
loom card_bytes=24553 card_bound=24576 reds_bytes=20208 folds=2
